---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Insights" description="Notes on Cameroonian and OHADA practice.">
<div>
  <section style="max-width:1360px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(48px,7vw,104px) clamp(20px,5vw,80px) clamp(32px,4vw,48px)">
    <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#007EA7;margin-bottom:28px">Insights</div>
    <h1 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:300;font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,64px);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;max-width:20ch">Notes on Cameroonian and OHADA practice</h1>
    <p style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#6b7b82;max-width:66ch;margin:28px 0 0">[Headlines below are proposed subjects. Publication dates and final copy to be confirmed by the firm.]</p>
  </section>
  <hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14);margin:0" />
  <section style="max-width:1360px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5vw,80px) clamp(56px,7vw,96px)">
    <a href="/insights/registering-security-at-the-rccm/" class="card" data-reveal="1" style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:none;border:0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14);padding:clamp(24px,3vw,36px) 0;cursor:pointer;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,minmax(0,1fr));gap:32px">
      <div style="grid-column:span 3;min-width:150px;font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12.5px;color:#6b7b82">[month year]<br />Finance</div>
      <div style="grid-column:span 8;min-width:260px"><h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(22px,2.2vw,29px);line-height:1.25;margin:0 0 10px;color:#00171F;max-width:34ch">Registering security at the RCCM: what lenders get wrong</h2><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4a5a61;max-width:62ch">Perfection under the Uniform Act on Secured Transactions is a registration question, and lapsed renewals are the most common reason a lender finds itself ranked behind a later interest.</p></div>
    </a>
    <div data-reveal="1" style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14);padding:clamp(24px,3vw,36px) 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,minmax(0,1fr));gap:32px">
      <div style="grid-column:span 3;min-width:150px;font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12.5px;color:#6b7b82">[month year]<br />Land</div>
      <div style="grid-column:span 8;min-width:260px"><h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(22px,2.2vw,29px);line-height:1.25;margin:0 0 10px;max-width:34ch">Customary tenure and registered title in the Southwest</h2><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4a5a61;max-width:62ch">What a buyer should do when a valid land certificate and a long-standing customary claim point to the same parcel.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div data-reveal="1" style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14);padding:clamp(24px,3vw,36px) 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,minmax(0,1fr));gap:32px">
      <div style="grid-column:span 3;min-width:150px;font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12.5px;color:#6b7b82">[month year]<br />Corporate</div>
      <div style="grid-column:span 8;min-width:260px"><h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(22px,2.2vw,29px);line-height:1.25;margin:0 0 10px;max-width:34ch">Choosing between an SA, a SARL and an SAS</h2><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4a5a61;max-width:62ch">How governance, transfer restrictions and audit obligations differ, and why the choice is expensive to revisit after trading begins.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div data-reveal="1" style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14);padding:clamp(24px,3vw,36px) 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,minmax(0,1fr));gap:32px">
      <div style="grid-column:span 3;min-width:150px;font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12.5px;color:#6b7b82">[month year]<br />Disputes</div>
      <div style="grid-column:span 8;min-width:260px"><h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(22px,2.2vw,29px);line-height:1.25;margin:0 0 10px;max-width:34ch">Drafting an arbitration clause that works in Cameroon</h2><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4a5a61;max-width:62ch">Seat, language, institution and interim relief — and how the CCJA’s role changes the calculation for cross-border contracts.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div data-reveal="1" style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14);padding:clamp(24px,3vw,36px) 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,minmax(0,1fr));gap:32px">
      <div style="grid-column:span 3;min-width:150px;font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12.5px;color:#6b7b82">[month year]<br />Succession</div>
      <div style="grid-column:span 8;min-width:260px"><h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(22px,2.2vw,29px);line-height:1.25;margin:0 0 10px;max-width:34ch">Estates that straddle borders: a note for diaspora families</h2><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4a5a61;max-width:62ch">Coordinating a Cameroonian grant with a foreign one, and untangling title that has passed informally through several generations.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
</Base>
